  <!-- PRIVACY POLICY -->

  <section
    class="scene"
    id="privacy"
    data-scene="privacy"
  >

    <section class="legal-page">

      <div class="container">
        <div class="legal-inner">

          <p class="eyebrow">
            Glowie
          </p>

          <h1>
            Privacy
            <span class="italic">Policy.</span>
          </h1>

          <p class="legal-date">
            Last updated: September 2026
          </p>


          <div class="legal-content">

            <p>
              This Privacy Policy explains how Glowsome s.r.o. ("Glowsome",
              "we", "us" or "our") collects, uses, stores and protects your
              personal data when you use Glowie.
            </p>


            <h2>
              1. Who we are
            </h2>

            <p>
              Glowie is operated by Glowsome s.r.o., U žlábku 174, Prague 5,
              155 31, Czech Republic, company ID 09021965.
            </p>

            <p>
              If you have questions about this Privacy Policy or the way your
              personal data is handled, you can contact us at
              <a href="mailto:glowie@glowsome.com">
                glowie@glowsome.com
              </a>.
            </p>


            <h2>
              2. What information we collect
            </h2>

            <p>
              Depending on how you use Glowie, we may collect and process the
              following categories of information:
            </p>

            <ul>
              <li>
                <strong>Conversation data:</strong> the messages and other
                information you choose to share while interacting with Glowie.
              </li>

              <li>
                <strong>Account information:</strong> information needed to
                create, maintain and manage your account.
              </li>

              <li>
                <strong>Device and usage information:</strong> technical
                information about how Glowie is accessed and used, including
                information necessary to maintain security, reliability and
                functionality.
              </li>
            </ul>

            <p>
              We do not require you to provide your name as part of your
              conversations with Glowie unless you choose to share it.
            </p>


            <h2>
              3. Why we process your information
            </h2>

            <p>
              Conversation data is used only to provide and personalise your
              Glowie experience, including maintaining appropriate context
              within your conversations.
            </p>

            <p>
              We do not use your conversation data to train AI models, sell
              advertising, sell your personal data or use your conversations
              for unrelated purposes.
            </p>

            <p>
              Account and usage information may be processed where necessary
              to provide the service under our contract with you and where
              necessary for our legitimate interests in operating, protecting
              and improving the reliability of Glowie.
            </p>

            <p>
              Where your conversations contain sensitive personal data, we
              process that information on the basis of your explicit consent.
            </p>


            <h2>
              4. Sensitive personal data
            </h2>

            <p>
              Because Glowie is designed as a space for personal reflection,
              you may choose to discuss sensitive topics such as relationships,
              emotions, sexuality or mental well-being.
            </p>

            <p>
              Some of this information may constitute special category
              personal data under the General Data Protection Regulation
              ("GDPR").
            </p>

            <p>
              By choosing to use Glowie and voluntarily sharing this
              information, you consent to its processing for the purpose of
              providing the Glowie service. You can withdraw your consent by
              deleting your account.
            </p>


            <h2>
              5. How and where your data is stored
            </h2>

            <p>
              We take privacy and security seriously. Core Glowie data is
              stored in the European Union.
            </p>

            <p>
              Our infrastructure includes Amazon Web Services in Frankfurt,
              Germany, and Pinecone infrastructure in Ireland.
            </p>

            <p>
              Data is encrypted in transit and at rest using appropriate
              technical safeguards.
            </p>

            <p>
              Glowsome personnel do not routinely have direct access to the
              content of your conversations. Conversation data is not used for
              AI model training.
            </p>


            <h2>
              6. International data transfers
            </h2>

            <p>
              We use BuddyPro as a service provider involved in delivering
              Glowie. BuddyPro and its sub-processors may process limited data
              required to provide the service.
            </p>

            <p>
              When Glowie generates an AI response, information may be
              transmitted temporarily to an AI provider. Some of these
              providers may process data outside the European Economic Area,
              including in the United States.
            </p>

            <p>
              Where personal data is transferred outside the European
              Economic Area, appropriate safeguards are used where required,
              including the European Commission's Standard Contractual
              Clauses under Decision 2021/914 or, where applicable,
              participation in the EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework.
            </p>

            <p>
              Core stored Glowie data remains within the European Union.
              Transfers to AI providers are transient and are used only to
              generate responses. Conversation data is not provided for model
              training.
            </p>

            <p>
              You can read BuddyPro's privacy information at
              <a
                href="https://buddypro.ai/privacy"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer"
              >
                buddypro.ai/privacy
              </a>
              and its terms at
              <a
                href="https://buddypro.ai/terms"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer"
              >
                buddypro.ai/terms
              </a>.
            </p>


            <h2>
              7. How long we keep your data
            </h2>

            <p>
              Your data is generally retained while your account remains
              active so that we can provide the Glowie service.
            </p>

            <p>
              If you delete your account, associated personal data is
              scheduled for deletion. Deletion is normally completed within
              a few days and, including relevant backups, within 30 days.
            </p>

            <p>
              If you need assistance with deletion, contact
              <a href="mailto:glowie@glowsome.com">
                glowie@glowsome.com
              </a>.
            </p>


            <h2>
              8. Your rights under GDPR
            </h2>

            <p>
              If the GDPR applies to you, you may have rights including the
              right to:
            </p>

            <ul>
              <li>request access to your personal data;</li>
              <li>request correction of inaccurate personal data;</li>
              <li>request deletion of your personal data;</li>
              <li>request restriction of processing;</li>
              <li>object to certain processing;</li>
              <li>
                receive portable copies of eligible account data; and
              </li>
              <li>
                withdraw consent where processing is based on consent.
              </li>
            </ul>

            <p>
              Conversation content is not provided as a downloadable export
              by design. You can, however, delete your conversation data and
              account.
            </p>

            <p>
              You also have the right to lodge a complaint with the relevant
              data protection authority.
            </p>


            <h2>
              9. Automated decision-making
            </h2>

            <p>
              Glowie does not use your personal data to make automated
              decisions that produce legal effects or similarly significant
              effects about you.
            </p>


            <h2>
              10. Third-party service providers
            </h2>

            <p>
              We rely on carefully selected service providers to operate
              Glowie. These may include:
            </p>

            <ul>
              <li>
                BuddyPro and its authorised sub-processors;
              </li>

              <li>
                AI service providers such as OpenAI, Anthropic, Google or
                OpenRouter where required to generate Glowie responses;
              </li>

              <li>
                Pinecone infrastructure in Ireland;
              </li>

              <li>
                Amazon Web Services infrastructure in Frankfurt, Germany;
              </li>

              <li>
                payment processing providers where payments are made outside
                Apple's App Store; and
              </li>

              <li>
                Apple, where subscriptions or purchases are made through the
                iOS App Store.
              </li>
            </ul>

            <p>
              A current list of BuddyPro sub-processors can be found at
              <a
                href="https://buddypro.ai/terms/sub-processors"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer"
              >
                buddypro.ai/terms/sub-processors
              </a>.
            </p>

            <p>
              We do not sell your personal data.
            </p>


            <h2>
              11. Glowie is not a medical or therapeutic service
            </h2>

            <p>
              Glowie is an AI companion designed to support reflection and
              self-exploration. It is not a medical service, psychotherapy,
              psychological treatment, diagnosis or crisis service.
            </p>

            <p>
              If you believe you or another person may be in immediate danger,
              experiencing a medical emergency or at risk of self-harm, contact
              your local emergency services or an appropriate crisis service
              immediately.
            </p>


            <h2>
              12. Children
            </h2>

            <p>
              Glowie is intended only for users aged 18 or over. We do not
              knowingly provide the service to children.
            </p>


            <h2>
              13. Changes to this Privacy Policy
            </h2>

            <p>
              We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time to reflect
              changes to Glowie, our service providers or applicable legal
              requirements.
            </p>

            <p>
              Where appropriate, we will make reasonable efforts to inform
              users of material changes.
            </p>


            <div class="legal-summary">

              <h2>
                Your privacy, in plain terms
              </h2>

              <p>
                Your conversations are there to make Glowie useful to you.
                They are not sold, used for advertising or used to train AI
                models.
              </p>

              <p>
                Core Glowie data is stored in the EU. Information may be sent
                temporarily to AI providers when necessary to generate a
                response, with appropriate data protection safeguards.
              </p>

              <p>
                You can delete your account and associated data, and you can
                contact us at
                <a href="mailto:glowie@glowsome.com">
                  glowie@glowsome.com
                </a>
                if you have questions about your privacy.
              </p>

            </div>


            <div class="legal-page-links">

              <a
                href="#terms"
                data-page="terms"
              >
                Terms of Service
                <span>↗</span>
              </a>

              <a
                href="#glowie"
                data-page="glowie"
              >
                Back to Glowie
                <span>↗</span>
              </a>

            </div>

          </div>

        </div>
      </div>

    </section>

  </section>  <!-- TERMS OF SERVICE -->

  <section
    class="scene"
    id="terms"
    data-scene="terms"
  >

    <section class="legal-page">

      <div class="container">
        <div class="legal-inner">

          <p class="eyebrow">
            Glowie
          </p>

          <h1>
            Terms of
            <span class="italic">Service.</span>
          </h1>

          <p class="legal-date">
            Last updated: September 2026
          </p>


          <div class="legal-content">

            <p>
              These Terms of Service ("Terms") govern your use of Glowie.
              By creating an account, purchasing a subscription or otherwise
              using Glowie, you agree to these Terms.
            </p>


            <h2>
              1. Who we are
            </h2>

            <p>
              Glowie is operated by Glowsome s.r.o., U žlábku 174, Prague 5,
              155 31, Czech Republic, company ID 09021965.
            </p>

            <p>
              You can contact us at
              <a href="mailto:glowie@glowsome.com">
                glowie@glowsome.com
              </a>.
            </p>


            <h2>
              2. What Glowie is
            </h2>

            <p>
              Glowie is an AI companion designed to support reflection,
              self-exploration and greater understanding of relationships.
              It uses conversational artificial intelligence informed by
              systemic therapy principles to provide a space for thoughtful,
              curious dialogue.
            </p>

            <p>
              Glowie is not psychotherapy, psychological treatment, medical
              treatment, diagnosis, professional counselling or a crisis
              service.
            </p>

            <p>
              Glowie does not replace a qualified therapist, psychologist,
              doctor or other healthcare professional. Responses generated by
              Glowie should not be treated as professional medical,
              psychological, legal or other professional advice.
            </p>

            <p>
              If you believe you or another person may be in immediate danger,
              experiencing a medical emergency or at risk of self-harm, contact
              your local emergency services or an appropriate crisis service
              immediately.
            </p>


            <h2>
              3. Age requirement
            </h2>

            <p>
              You must be at least 18 years old to use Glowie.
            </p>

            <p>
              By creating an account or using the service, you confirm that
              you are 18 years of age or older and legally able to enter into
              these Terms.
            </p>


            <h2>
              4. Subscriptions, message allowances and payments
            </h2>

            <p>
              Glowie may be offered through paid subscriptions and additional
              message packages.
            </p>

            <p>
              The available plans are:
            </p>

            <ul>
              <li>
                <strong>Monthly subscription:</strong>
                300 messages per month for €70.
              </li>

              <li>
                <strong>Quarterly subscription:</strong>
                300 messages per month for three months for €189.
              </li>

              <li>
                <strong>Additional message package:</strong>
                a one-time purchase of 500 additional messages for €117.
                Additional message packages do not expire but require an
                active subscription to use.
              </li>
            </ul>

            <p>
              Both messages you send and messages generated by Glowie count
              towards your message allowance. A monthly allowance of 300
              messages therefore represents approximately 150 conversational
              exchanges, depending on how you use the service. A package of
              500 additional messages represents approximately 250
              conversational exchanges.
            </p>

            <p>
              Your monthly message allowance resets at the beginning of each
              new subscription period. Unused monthly messages do not carry
              over into the following month.
            </p>

            <p>
              Purchased additional messages do not expire and are used after
              the monthly allowance included with your active subscription
              has been used.
            </p>


            <h3>
              App Store purchases
            </h3>

            <p>
              Where you subscribe or make a purchase through Apple's App
              Store, payment is charged to your Apple ID account at
              confirmation of purchase.
            </p>

            <p>
              Prices displayed in the App Store may vary by country or region
              and may include applicable taxes or local pricing adjustments.
              The price displayed by Apple at the time of purchase is the
              price that applies to your transaction.
            </p>


            <h3>
              Automatic renewal
            </h3>

            <p>
              Subscriptions purchased through Apple's App Store automatically
              renew unless auto-renewal is turned off at least 24 hours before
              the end of the current subscription period.
            </p>

            <p>
              Your Apple ID account may be charged for renewal within 24 hours
              before the end of the current subscription period.
            </p>

            <p>
              You can manage or cancel your subscription through your Apple ID
              subscription settings.
            </p>


            <h2>
              5. Cancellation, refunds and right of withdrawal
            </h2>

            <p>
              You can cancel an App Store subscription at any time through
              your Apple subscription settings. Cancellation prevents future
              renewals but does not normally end access for a subscription
              period that has already been paid for.
            </p>

            <p>
              Where your purchase was made through Apple's App Store, refund
              requests are handled by Apple and are subject to Apple's
              applicable terms and refund policies. You can request a refund
              from Apple at
              <a
                href="https://reportaproblem.apple.com/"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer"
              >
                reportaproblem.apple.com
              </a>.
            </p>

            <p>
              If you are a consumer in the European Union or European Economic
              Area, you may have a statutory right to withdraw from certain
              distance contracts within 14 days.
            </p>

            <p>
              Where you expressly request immediate access to digital content
              or a digital service and acknowledge that providing the service
              may affect or end your statutory withdrawal right, the right of
              withdrawal may no longer apply once performance has begun, to
              the extent permitted by applicable law.
            </p>

            <p>
              Nothing in these Terms removes consumer rights that cannot
              lawfully be excluded or limited.
            </p>


            <h2>
              6. Acceptable use
            </h2>

            <p>
              You agree to use Glowie lawfully and responsibly.
            </p>

            <p>
              You must not:
            </p>

            <ul>
              <li>
                use Glowie in violation of applicable laws or regulations;
              </li>

              <li>
                attempt to gain unauthorised access to Glowie, its systems,
                accounts or infrastructure;
              </li>

              <li>
                interfere with, damage, overload or disrupt the service or its
                security features;
              </li>

              <li>
                reverse engineer, scrape, systematically extract or reproduce
                the service except where applicable law expressly permits it;
              </li>

              <li>
                use Glowie to infringe the rights, privacy or intellectual
                property of another person;
              </li>

              <li>
                impersonate another person or misrepresent your identity in a
                way intended to deceive or cause harm; or
              </li>

              <li>
                use the service for fraudulent, abusive or unlawful purposes.
              </li>
